+# Beneficial particle-use gate follow-up
+
+The original three assertion paths accepted
+`abs(zero_code_minus_live) > 1e-6`. Lower common game loss is better, so this
+accepted particle codes that worsened the game. The runner, recovered scorer
+and tensor-based learned regression now require the signed delta to exceed
+`1e-6` under every mandatory common critic.
+
+The new software control supplies a harmful code effect under each of the four
+judges in turn, while preserving positive initialization improvements and all
+other tensor ownership/restoration assertions. Each must be rejected. A
+positive control must pass. Its three-update fixtures and synthetic scores are
+software tests, with no full-horizon training or qualification credit.
+
+The recovered scorer's source proof now admits exactly two evaluation changes:
+the fresh checkpoint carrier and this signed classification gate. It records
+the archived training gate as `unsigned_effect_v1` and the new evaluated gate
+as `beneficial_signed_v2`. Other source changes still fail preflight. Archived
+training bindings, failed receipts, curves and checkpoints retain their actual
+identities; they are not relabelled as training performed under this new source.
+
+The existing measured endpoint deltas are all positive:
+`0.755647 / 0.584848 / 1.185280 / 0.930370` in the declared judge order. They
+therefore support beneficial particle use under the stronger signed check.
+No unchanged campaign should be retrained only to alter this classification.
+
+```sh
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 python -m pytest -q \
+    tests/test_e22_routed_convergence.py \
+    tests/test_e22_routed_convergence_neutral.py \
+    tests/test_e22_routed_convergence_signed_gate.py \
+    tests/test_e22_routed_convergence_long.py
+```
+
+The original opt-in full-training regression remains separate. Its exact current
+revision and required CI checks must be verified before merging; the saved
+diagnostic is not a Supra quality or Forge qualification.
